cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Veraxi in research, please cite it as below."
title: "Veraxi"
abstract: >-
  An evidence-first research workbench built on a Hybrid GraphRAG engine
  (Neo4j knowledge graph + Qdrant dense/sparse vector search, fused via
  Reciprocal Rank Fusion), with machine-verified citations, code
  intelligence, and security-graph analysis. FastAPI/Python backend and
  a cross-platform Flutter client, exposed to LLMs over MCP with BYOK
  and local-model support.
authors:
  - family-names: "Coaguila"
    given-names: "Kazuo"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kcoaguila-dev/veraxi"
license: "MIT"
keywords:
  - graphrag
  - retrieval-augmented-generation
  - code-intelligence
  - application-security
  - model-context-protocol
